[2026-02-04T17:32:27.032Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GKvK7DnCKEZX92KLbYo1oc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tech layoffs January 2026 25000 jobs global startup tracker statistics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"9 Trends Shaping Work in 2026 and Beyond\",\"url\":\"https://hbr.org/2026/02/9-trends-shaping-work-in-2026-and-beyond\"},{\"title\":\"Global tech and startup layoffs hit 25,000 in January as AI spending and cost cuts accelerate - BusinessToday\",\"url\":\"https://www.businesstoday.in/technology/news/story/one-month-into-2026-global-tech-and-startup-layoffs-near-25000-514445-2026-02-03\"},{\"title\":\"Layoffs Tracker - All Tech and Startup Layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.trueup.io/layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"2026 tech company layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.informationweek.com/it-staffing-careers/2026-tech-company-layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Tech Layoffs: US Companies With Job Cuts In 2024 And 2025\",\"url\":\"https://news.crunchbase.com/startups/tech-layoffs/\"},{\"title\":\"Tech layoffs roundup: Every major company cutting jobs in 2025-2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.androidheadlines.com/2026/01/tech-layoffs-roundup-every-major-company-cutting-jobs-in-2025-2026.html\"},{\"title\":\"Layoffs Tracker 2026: Real-Time Company Layoffs Data\",\"url\":\"https://www.interviewpal.com/layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Layoffs.fyi - Tech and Startup Layoff Tracker\",\"url\":\"https://layoffs.fyi/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon's layoffs are staggering. We've seen this before\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnn.com/2026/01/31/tech/amazon-layoffs-january-tech-changes\"},{\"title\":\"A comprehensive list of 2025 tech layoffs | TechCrunch\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/12/22/tech-layoffs-2025-list/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key statistics about tech layoffs in January 2026:\n\n## January 2026 Layoff Statistics\n\nAccording to layoff-tracking website Layoffs.fyi, tech and startup job cuts reached 24,818 across 27 companies worldwide as of January. Global technology companies and startups cut nearly 25,000 jobs in January, extending a multiyear wave of layoffs into 2026 as firms redirect spending toward artificial intelligence (AI), cloud infrastructure and data centres while trimming costs elsewhere.\n\n## Major Companies Affected\n\nSome of the biggest cuts came from Amazon, which laid off about 16,000 employees on January 28, and Meta announced 1,500 job cuts, about 10% of its Reality Labs division.\n\n## Drivers of Layoffs\n\nMuch of the downsizing reflects a shift in capital allocation as companies pour money into AI. Budgets are being redirected toward AI models, graphics processing units, cloud infrastructure and large-scale data centres. Beyond the AI pivot, layoffs are also being driven by investor pressure to improve cash flow, or by efforts to streamline operations and lift profitability.\n\n## Future Outlook\n\nOracle is said to be planning as many as 30,000 layoffs to help fund expanded data-centre investments, suggesting the trend could persist through the year.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"637ed760-5ff1-492b-9369-4da7ad6de268","tool_use_result":{"query":"tech layoffs January 2026 25000 jobs global startup tracker statistics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014xhpX1mYnLqBpPrAJqC6Sb","content":[{"title":"9 Trends Shaping Work in 2026 and Beyond","url":"https://hbr.org/2026/02/9-trends-shaping-work-in-2026-and-beyond"},{"title":"Global tech and startup layoffs hit 25,000 in January as AI spending and cost cuts accelerate - BusinessToday","url":"https://www.businesstoday.in/technology/news/story/one-month-into-2026-global-tech-and-startup-layoffs-near-25000-514445-2026-02-03"},{"title":"Layoffs Tracker - All Tech and Startup Layoffs","url":"https://www.trueup.io/layoffs"},{"title":"2026 tech company layoffs","url":"https://www.informationweek.com/it-staffing-careers/2026-tech-company-layoffs"},{"title":"Tech Layoffs: US Companies With Job Cuts In 2024 And 2025","url":"https://news.crunchbase.com/startups/tech-layoffs/"},{"title":"Tech layoffs roundup: Every major company cutting jobs in 2025-2026","url":"https://www.androidheadlines.com/2026/01/tech-layoffs-roundup-every-major-company-cutting-jobs-in-2025-2026.html"},{"title":"Layoffs Tracker 2026: Real-Time Company Layoffs Data","url":"https://www.interviewpal.com/layoffs"},{"title":"Layoffs.fyi - Tech and Startup Layoff Tracker","url":"https://layoffs.fyi/"},{"title":"Amazon's layoffs are staggering. We've seen this before","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/01/31/tech/amazon-layoffs-january-tech-changes"},{"title":"A comprehensive list of 2025 tech layoffs | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2025/12/22/tech-layoffs-2025-list/"}]},"Based on the search results, here are the key statistics about tech layoffs in January 2026:\n\n## January 2026 Layoff Statistics\n\nAccording to layoff-tracking website Layoffs.fyi, tech and startup job cuts reached 24,818 across 27 companies worldwide as of January. Global technology companies and startups cut nearly 25,000 jobs in January, extending a multiyear wave of layoffs into 2026 as firms redirect spending toward artificial intelligence (AI), cloud infrastructure and data centres while trimming costs elsewhere.\n\n## Major Companies Affected\n\nSome of the biggest cuts came from Amazon, which laid off about 16,000 employees on January 28, and Meta announced 1,500 job cuts, about 10% of its Reality Labs division.\n\n## Drivers of Layoffs\n\nMuch of the downsizing reflects a shift in capital allocation as companies pour money into AI. Budgets are being redirected toward AI models, graphics processing units, cloud infrastructure and large-scale data centres. Beyond the AI pivot, layoffs are also being driven by investor pressure to improve cash flow, or by efforts to streamline operations and lift profitability.\n\n## Future Outlook\n\nOracle is said to be planning as many as 30,000 layoffs to help fund expanded data-centre investments, suggesting the trend could persist through the year."],"durationSeconds":7.2423516999999995}}
