[2026-02-04T17:33:34.838Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MZLVJmv54sceSHEesgWss4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tech layoffs 2022 2023 2024 2025 comparison annual statistics historical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Tech Layoffs: US Companies With Job Cuts In 2024 And 2025\",\"url\":\"https://news.crunchbase.com/startups/tech-layoffs/\"},{\"title\":\"Tech layoffs by quarter worldwide 2020-2024 | Statista\",\"url\":\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/199999/worldwide-tech-layoffs-covid-19/\"},{\"title\":\"Tech sector layoffs explained: What you need to know\",\"url\":\"https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/feature/Tech-sector-layoffs-explained-What-you-need-to-know\"},{\"title\":\"Layoffs.fyi - Tech and Startup Layoff Tracker\",\"url\":\"https://layoffs.fyi/\"},{\"title\":\"Tech Layoffs in 2025 - NerdWallet\",\"url\":\"https://www.nerdwallet.com/article/finance/tech-layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Biggest tech layoffs since COVID-19 worldwide 2020-2023 | Statista\",\"url\":\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/1127080/worldwide-tech-layoffs-covid-19-biggest/\"},{\"title\":\"Data: Tech Layoffs Remain Stubbornly High, With Big Tech Leading The Way\",\"url\":\"https://news.crunchbase.com/layoffs/big-tech-leads-workforce-cuts-msft-amzn/\"},{\"title\":\"A comprehensive list of 2025 tech layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/comprehensive-list-2025-tech-layoffs-134836336.html\"},{\"title\":\"Major Tech Layoffs in 2025: An Updated Tracker\",\"url\":\"https://www.informationweek.com/it-leadership/tech-company-layoffs-the-covid-tech-bubble-bursts-sep-14\"},{\"title\":\"50 Latest Layoff Statistics 2026 (Global Data)\",\"url\":\"https://www.demandsage.com/layoff-statistics/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of tech layoffs across 2022-2025:\n\n## Annual Statistics\n\n**2022:** Tech layoffs started surging in 2022 with an estimated 93,000 U.S. tech workers laid off that year, while a record number of 263 thousand laid off employees occurred in the global tech sector by the end of 2022.\n\n**2023:** Around 200,000 U.S. tech employees were laid off in 2023, more than double the 2022 figure. Globally, the first quarter of 2023 saw a record high of 167.6 thousand employees losing their jobs, with peak of 585 companies in the first quarter of 2023.\n\n**2024:** Layoffs declined in 2024 compared to the previous year, with at least 95,000 workers at U.S.-based tech companies laid off in mass job cuts in 2024.\n\n**2025:** Over 206,101 employees were laid off from 221 tech companies in the United States, with job cuts increasing by 5.9% compared to 2024. Intel laid off the most employees in 2025, removing 24,000 employees.\n\n## Key Trends\n\nTech layoffs noticeably increased at the start of 2022, ramped up in 2023, waned somewhat in 2024 and have continued in 2025. In 2022 and 2023 combined, 428,449 people working for tech companies were laid off.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"8d14bc4b-4dd7-4d75-bf81-0f7fd7aca577","tool_use_result":{"query":"tech layoffs 2022 2023 2024 2025 comparison annual statistics historical","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BBpESGX4zYRsY8yrjuFcDE","content":[{"title":"Tech Layoffs: US Companies With Job Cuts In 2024 And 2025","url":"https://news.crunchbase.com/startups/tech-layoffs/"},{"title":"Tech layoffs by quarter worldwide 2020-2024 | Statista","url":"https://www.statista.com/statistics/199999/worldwide-tech-layoffs-covid-19/"},{"title":"Tech sector layoffs explained: What you need to know","url":"https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/feature/Tech-sector-layoffs-explained-What-you-need-to-know"},{"title":"Layoffs.fyi - Tech and Startup Layoff Tracker","url":"https://layoffs.fyi/"},{"title":"Tech Layoffs in 2025 - NerdWallet","url":"https://www.nerdwallet.com/article/finance/tech-layoffs"},{"title":"Biggest tech layoffs since COVID-19 worldwide 2020-2023 | Statista","url":"https://www.statista.com/statistics/1127080/worldwide-tech-layoffs-covid-19-biggest/"},{"title":"Data: Tech Layoffs Remain Stubbornly High, With Big Tech Leading The Way","url":"https://news.crunchbase.com/layoffs/big-tech-leads-workforce-cuts-msft-amzn/"},{"title":"A comprehensive list of 2025 tech layoffs","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/comprehensive-list-2025-tech-layoffs-134836336.html"},{"title":"Major Tech Layoffs in 2025: An Updated Tracker","url":"https://www.informationweek.com/it-leadership/tech-company-layoffs-the-covid-tech-bubble-bursts-sep-14"},{"title":"50 Latest Layoff Statistics 2026 (Global Data)","url":"https://www.demandsage.com/layoff-statistics/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of tech layoffs across 2022-2025:\n\n## Annual Statistics\n\n**2022:** Tech layoffs started surging in 2022 with an estimated 93,000 U.S. tech workers laid off that year, while a record number of 263 thousand laid off employees occurred in the global tech sector by the end of 2022.\n\n**2023:** Around 200,000 U.S. tech employees were laid off in 2023, more than double the 2022 figure. Globally, the first quarter of 2023 saw a record high of 167.6 thousand employees losing their jobs, with peak of 585 companies in the first quarter of 2023.\n\n**2024:** Layoffs declined in 2024 compared to the previous year, with at least 95,000 workers at U.S.-based tech companies laid off in mass job cuts in 2024.\n\n**2025:** Over 206,101 employees were laid off from 221 tech companies in the United States, with job cuts increasing by 5.9% compared to 2024. Intel laid off the most employees in 2025, removing 24,000 employees.\n\n## Key Trends\n\nTech layoffs noticeably increased at the start of 2022, ramped up in 2023, waned somewhat in 2024 and have continued in 2025. In 2022 and 2023 combined, 428,449 people working for tech companies were laid off."],"durationSeconds":6.819736100000009}}
